# Build-context trim for the agent-tools images (containers/agent-tools/,
# issue #203). The build context is the repo root because the images' labctl
# stage compiles labctl from the Go working tree — it needs go.mod/go.sum and
# the cmd/ + internal/ tree (with its embedded assets), but NOT .git, the
# compiled binaries, or the web SPA's node_modules/dist. labctl builds untagged
# (no `-tags ui`), so it uses internal/webui's placeholder variant and never
# reaches internal/webui/dist — safe to drop. Keeping the context lean speeds
# the COPY and avoids shipping build outputs into the image build.
.git
bin
web/node_modules
web/dist
internal/webui/dist
.claude
